Indeed, consider x ∈ AZ with a defect x01 = 00. The phase of the 0 in position 0 is 0 and the phase
of the 0 in position 1 is 1, so this corresponds to a particle p01 . Changing the position of the defect
would not change the particle since the local phase would be modified accordingly.
   The update function is defined in the intuitive manner: with p01 evolving at speed +1 and p10
at speed −1 and both particles being sent to ∅ in case of collision.
