See Figure 1 for an example of space-time diagram.

   This automaton was introduced by [Fis90b]. In this paper, the author shows that for all Bernoulli
measure µ, the set [i]0 (for i ∈ A) is a µ-attractor iff n ≥ 5: that is, µ({x ∈ AZ : ∃T ∈ N, ∀t ≥
T, F t x ∈ [i]}) > 0 for all i. Simulations starting from a random configuration suggest the following:
for n = 3 or 4, monochromatic regions keep increasing in size; for n ≥ 5, we observe the convergence
to a fixed point where small regions are delimited by vertical lines. We use the main result to
explain this observation.
