3.2. Entry times
The main result of Section 2 implies that, for any σ-ergodic initial measure µ, ΛG (µ) contains at
most one kind of particle, which one depending on whether µ([+1]) > µ([−1]) or the opposite.
When µ([+1]) = µ([−1]), ΛG (µ) only contains the particle-free configuration ∞ 0∞ . In other words,
Gt∗ µ → δb0 , which means that the probability of seeing a particle in any fixed finite window tends to
0 as t → ∞.
Definition 11 (Entry times). Let v− < 0 ≤ v+ ∈ Z, G the (v− , v+ )-GA and x ∈ {−1, 0, 1}Z . We
define:
                  Tn− (x) = min{k ∈ N : ∃i ∈ [0, |v− | − 1], Gk+n (x)i = −1},
 with Tn− (x) = ∞ if this set is empty. This is the entry time in the set {b ∈ {−1, 0, 1}Z : ∃i ∈
[0, |v− | − 1], bi = −1} after time n at position 0 starting from x. We define Tn+ (x) in a symmetrical
manner.
