3.4. Particle density
Definition 13 (Particle density in a configuration). The −1 particle density in x ∈ {−1, 0, 1}Z is
defined as d− (x) = Freq(−1, x). d+ (x) is defined in a symmetrical manner.
  In all the following, any result on d− also holds for d+ by symmetry.
Theorem 6 (Decrease rate of the particle density). Let G be a (v− , v+ )-GA with initial measure
