      known (e.g. starting from the uniform measure), Theorem 7 does not apply directly.
     One-sided captive automata: Let F be any one-sided captive cellular automaton defined
      by a local rule f . As explained in Section 2.6, F factorises onto the (−1, 0)-gliders automaton
      with a factor defined by:
                                  ab →
